course: dictionary
lesson: 6295
title: Learning a noun from its clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A noun names a thing, such as a bird, a pond or a river. When you meet a new noun, look for clues in the sentence. «In winter the ducks stand on the ice, and two black birds argue at the edge: a coot with a white beak, and a moorhen with a red and yellow beak.» The sentence tells you a moorhen is a black bird with a red and yellow beak.
explain: Sentences that compare two things are very helpful. «A coot is a black water bird with a white beak, and a moorhen is a black bird with a red and yellow beak.» The birds look alike, so the difference is the clue: the beak colour. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does "a moorhen is a black bird with a red and yellow beak" still make sense? Yes, so you have it right.
explain: Some words tell you where to find a thing. «The bank is so busy with otters, kingfishers and moorhens that he's never lonely.» Moorhens live on the riverbank with other animals. A dictionary adds more: a moorhen is often seen on ponds, rivers and canals.
fact: A moorhen is a black water bird with a red and yellow beak.
fact: A moorhen has a white stripe on its side.
fact: Moorhens are often seen on ponds, rivers and canals.
fact: Moorhens swim with jerking heads and walk on floating plants with long green toes.
fact: A coot is similar to a moorhen, but it has a white beak.
exercise: «A coot is a black water bird with a white beak, and a moorhen is a black bird with a red and yellow beak.» What colour is a moorhen's beak? | *Red and yellow | Green and blue | White | Black
exercise: Sam sees a moorhen swimming on a pond. Where might Sam find a moorhen? | *On a pond, river or canal | Inside a house | On a mountain covered in snow | In a desert
exercise: «In winter the ducks stand on the ice, and two black birds argue at the edge: a coot with a white beak and a moorhen with a red and yellow beak.» Which bird has a white beak? | A kingfisher | *A coot | A duck | A moorhen
test: Tom says a moorhen is a fish. What is a moorhen really? | *A bird | A stone | A plant | Fish
test: Where is a moorhen's white stripe? | On its head | On its back | On its tail | *On its side
exam: «A coot is a black water bird with a white beak, and a moorhen is a black bird with a red and yellow beak.» Which two birds are alike, and how can you tell them apart? | Coot and dabchick; both have red beaks | Moorhen and kingfisher; both dive for fish | *Coot and moorhen; the coot has a white beak and the moorhen a red and yellow beak | Ducks and moorhens; both stand on the ice
